        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.135,
            0.884,
            0.217
          ],
          "content": "For measuring temperature, the clinical thermometers generally use a scale called the **Celsius scale**. On this scale, the unit of temperature is **degree Celsius** and is denoted by °C."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.262,
            0.795,
            0.344
          ],
          "content": "Earlier, mercury thermometers were used for measuring the body temperature. But mercury is an extremely toxic substance and is difficult to dispose of if the thermometer breaks accidently."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.451,
            0.348,
            0.738,
            0.382
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_3_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.4,
            0.754,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": "Digital thermometers pose no such risk and also the numbers in its display are easier to read. Therefore, mercury thermometers are being replaced by digital thermometers. Temperature in a digital thermometer is determined with the help of heat sensors."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.787,
            0.478,
            0.859,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": "",
